{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed.</b> In my opinion, the pillar of cloud that went before them when they went out of Egypt, and the pillar of fire likewise by night — to travel by day and by night (above, 13:21) — but after Pharaoh and his army drowned, they had no fear, and they would not travel by night. Now you will not find in the section BeHa'alotkha that they traveled by night. And Moses set them journeying at HaShem's command, and they are only six journeys until Mount Sinai, and they are fewer than forty days, and the air was good — neither damp nor cold — and whoever had no tent could stand in the air and it would not harm him. And when they came to the wilderness of Sinai they all made booths, for there they would remain until they made the Tabernacle, for this reason he brought acacia wood out of Egypt, as I shall explain. And as a remembrance of the booths they made there was the festival of Sukkot, for Scripture says, 'for in booths I settled the children of Israel' (Leviticus 23:43) — and how could they have dwelt in clouds? For booths are not like clouds. I shall further explain why the festival of Sukkot is in the seventh month. And when the Tabernacle was made, HaShem descended in a pillar of cloud upon it, as it is written, 'and fire was by night in it' (below, 40:38), and when the cloud journeyed, the children of Israel would journey. And for this reason it is written, 'and in a pillar of cloud You go before them by day' (Numbers 14:14). Now there are two pillars that alternate over the Tabernacle. And if there is a tradition that there were seven clouds of glory, we set aside our reasoning and rely on the tradition." "<b>To the wilderness of Shur.</b> It is a wilderness by that name itself. Perhaps there were two cities in the wilderness called thus, or the wilderness has two names. And the proof that he said, 'and they went three days in the wilderness' — it is the wilderness of Shur; therefore the statement opens with a bet: במדבר (in the wilderness). 'And they found no water.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:54.740254013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}